# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-23
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\eta_j$ = quasi-probabilities\n"
msgstr "$\\eta_j$ = kvazipravděpodobnosti\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Some $\\eta_j < 0$\n"
msgstr "Some $\\eta_j < 0$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-23
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is the core idea behind PEC:\n"
msgstr "To je základní myšlenka PEC:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-23
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample channels according to $|\\eta_j|$∣\n"
msgstr "Vzorkuj kanály podle $|\\eta_j|$∣\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-23
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Attach signs to measurement outcomes\n"
msgstr "Připoj znaménka k výsledkům měření\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-23
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Expectation values converge to the noise-free value\n"
msgstr "Očekávané hodnoty konvergují k hodnotě bez šumu\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-23
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We apply PEC \"by hand\" to the estimation of $\\langle Z \\rangle$ by using the density matrix $\\rho_\\text{noisy}$ and see if we can recover the results for $\\rho_\\text{ideal}$. For $\\rho_\\text{ideal}$ we expect:\n"
msgstr "Aplikujeme PEC „ručně“ na odhad $\\langle Z \\rangle$ pomocí matice hustoty $\\rho_\\text{noisy}$ a uvidíme, zda dokážeme obnovit výsledky pro $\\rho_\\text{ideal}$. Pro $\\rho_\\text{ideal}$ očekáváme:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{ideal} & =\\text{Tr}(Z \\rho_\\text{ideal})\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & -\\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"&=\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\\\\n"
"&=0.5\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{ideal} & =\\text{Tr}(Z \\rho_\\text{ideal})\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & -\\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"&=\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\\\\n"
"&=0.5\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-23
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note also that for the noisy density matrix, we obtain:\n"
msgstr "Všimni si také, že pro zašuměnou matici hustoty dostaneme:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{noisy} & =\\text{Tr}\\left(Z \\rho_\\text{noisy}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"-0.346 & -0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"&=0.7-0.3\\\\\n"
"&=0.4\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{noisy} & =\\text{Tr}\\left(Z \\rho_\\text{noisy}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"-0.346 & -0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"&=0.7-0.3\\\\\n"
"&=0.4\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-23
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It's the right order of magnitude but significantly far from the ideal case.\n"
msgstr "Je to správný řád, ale podstatně se to liší od ideálního případu.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-23
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we step through how, with the PEC process, we can reconstruct the unbiased expectation value from the noisy density matrix. In real workflows, this is probabilistic and will be automated. In this \"by-hand\" workflow, we will choose probabilistic values that are realistic, but perhaps convenient for our presentation. This should not be taken as a claim that PEC is perfect. This is simply to show you a plausible scenario that could happen inside the PEC packages.\n"
msgstr "Nyní si projdeme, jak můžeme pomocí procesu PEC rekonstruovat nezkreslenou očekávanou hodnotu ze zašuměné matice hustoty. Ve skutečných pracovních postupech je to pravděpodobnostní a automatizované. V tomto „ručním“ postupu zvolíme pravděpodobnostní hodnoty, které jsou realistické, ale možná vhodné pro naši prezentaci. Neber to jako tvrzení, že PEC je dokonalé. Jde jen o ukázku věrohodného scénáře, který by se mohl odehrát uvnitř balíčků PEC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-23
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recall that our noise channel is of the form:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E} = (1 - p)\\mathcal{I} + \\frac{p}{3}(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
"The inverse can be written (exactly):\n"
msgstr ""
"Připomeňme, že náš šumový kanál má tvar:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E} = (1 - p)\\mathcal{I} + \\frac{p}{3}(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
"Inverzi lze zapsat (přesně):\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\alpha\\,\\mathcal{I} + \\beta(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
"based on symmetry of the transformation and the completeness of the Pauli operators. Inverting the noise channel somehow in the estimation process should yield an estimator that is unbiased and normalized. To do this, we must at least determine the coefficents $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ and then think about how to implement the inverse transformation. When done by a noise learner, the inversion of this noise channel would be done at the channel level, independent of a specific case like our density matrix. The coefficients $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ would come from this inversion.\n"
msgstr ""
"\\alpha\\,\\mathcal{I} + \\beta(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
"based on symmetry of the transformation and the completeness of the Pauli operators. Inverting the noise channel somehow in the estimation process should yield an estimator that is unbiased and normalized. To do this, we must at least determine the coefficents $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ and then think about how to implement the inverse transformation. When done by a noise learner, the inversion of this noise channel would be done at the channel level, independent of a specific case like our density matrix. The coefficients $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ would come from this inversion.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-23
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is simpler for this introduction to focus on the channel's effect on our density matrix. This allows us to work with familiar objects like density matrices and expectation values. To that end, consider what must be true about the effects of this inverse operation on our estimation process: the estimator produced by PEC must be normalized and unbiased. This corresponds to two conditions:\n"
msgstr "Pro tento úvod je jednodušší soustředit se na vliv kanálu na naši matici hustoty. Díky tomu můžeme pracovat se známými objekty, jako jsou matice hustoty a očekávané hodnoty. Proto uvažuj, co musí platit o účincích této inverzní operace na náš proces odhadu: estimátor vytvořený PEC musí být normalizovaný a nezkreslený. Odpovídá to dvěma podmínkám:\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-23
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Normalization: To ensure that this operation does not change the scale of the observable, we require that $\\alpha+3\\beta = 1$. To see why this is the case, we could either consider the action of the inverse on a density matrix, or consider its action on the expectation value of something trivial like $\\mathcal{I}$ itself.\n"
msgstr "Normalizace: Aby tato operace neměnila měřítko pozorovatelné, požadujeme $\\alpha+3\\beta = 1$. Abychom pochopili, proč tomu tak je, můžeme uvažovat působení inverze na matici hustoty, nebo její působení na očekávanou hodnotu něčeho triviálního, jako je samotné $\\mathcal{I}$.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-23
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calibration: In a real workflow, we use calibration circuits to learn noise behavior at a gate level. We then use the gate-level knowledge of noise behavior, and the linearity of expectation values to apply the learned noise model to the larger circuit. In our case, we started with artificial knowledge that the ideal expectation value $\\langle Z \\rangle = 0.5$. But it would be very easy to come up with a state for which we know theoretically that this would be the ideal value, and then use actual measurements for calibration. A key point is that for PEC, one typically does not learn a full noise model of the entire circuit. Instead, one learns local noise models for individual gates or circuit layers and uses those to construct the quasi-probability decomposition.\n"
msgstr "Kalibrace: Ve skutečném pracovním postupu používáme kalibrační obvody, abychom poznali chování šumu na úrovni hradel. Poté využijeme znalost chování šumu na úrovni hradel a linearitu očekávaných hodnot k aplikaci naučeného modelu šumu na větší obvod. V našem případě jsme vyšli z umělé znalosti, že ideální očekávaná hodnota je $\\langle Z \\rangle = 0.5$. Bylo by ale velmi snadné vymyslet stav, u kterého teoreticky víme, že by to byla ideální hodnota, a pak použít skutečná měření ke kalibraci. Klíčové je, že u PEC se typicky nenaučí úplný model šumu celého obvodu. Místo toho se učí lokální modely šumu pro jednotlivá hradla nebo vrstvy obvodu a ty se použijí k sestavení kvazipravděpodobnostního rozkladu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-23
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We use these conditions to determine $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$. We consider the ansatz\n"
msgstr "Pomocí těchto podmínek určíme $\\alpha$ a $\\beta$. Uvažujeme ansatz\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\alpha\\,\\mathcal{I} + \\beta(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z}),\n"
"$$\n"
"and apply it to an arbitrary single-qubit density matrix $\\rho$.\n"
msgstr ""
"\\alpha\\,\\mathcal{I} + \\beta(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z}),\n"
"$$\n"
"and apply it to an arbitrary single-qubit density matrix $\\rho$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-23
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recall that the Pauli channels act by conjugation:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{X}(\\rho) = X\\rho X, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{Y}(\\rho) = Y\\rho Y, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{Z}(\\rho) = Z\\rho Z.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Připomeňme, že Pauliho kanály působí konjugací:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{X}(\\rho) = X\\rho X, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{Y}(\\rho) = Y\\rho Y, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{Z}(\\rho) = Z\\rho Z.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-23
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Applying $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ to $\\rho$ gives:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Aplikací $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ na $\\rho$ dostaneme:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\alpha\\,\\rho\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta\\left(X\\rho X + Y\\rho Y + Z\\rho Z\\right).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\alpha\\,\\rho\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta\\left(X\\rho X + Y\\rho Y + Z\\rho Z\\right).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-23
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Taking the trace, we obtain:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"&=\n"
"\\alpha\\,\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta\\Big(\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(X\\rho X)\n"
"+\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(Y\\rho Y)\n"
"+\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(Z\\rho Z)\n"
"\\Big).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Vezmeme-li stopu, dostaneme:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"&=\n"
"\\alpha\\,\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta\\Big(\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(X\\rho X)\n"
"+\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(Y\\rho Y)\n"
"+\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(Z\\rho Z)\n"
"\\Big).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-23
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each Pauli operator is unitary, such that conjugation preserves the trace:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(P\\rho P) = \\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho),\n"
"\\qquad P \\in \\{X,Y,Z\\}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Každý Pauliho operátor je unitární, takže konjugace zachovává stopu:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(P\\rho P) = \\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho),\n"
"\\qquad P \\in \\{X,Y,Z\\}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Therefore,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Therefore,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(\\alpha + 3\\beta)\\,\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"(\\alpha + 3\\beta)\\,\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-23
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the PEC estimator to be normalized, the effective\n"
"inverse map must preserve the trace of all density matrices. That is, we require:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Aby byl estimátor PEC normalizovaný, musí efektivní\n"
"inverzní zobrazení zachovávat stopu všech matic hustoty. To znamená, že požadujeme:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho)\n"
"\\qquad \\text{for all } \\rho.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho)\n"
"\\qquad \\text{for all } \\rho.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-23
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This implies the normalization constraint:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\alpha + 3\\beta = 1.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Z toho plyne normalizační podmínka:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\alpha + 3\\beta = 1.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-23
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "But in our case, this yields the condition:\n"
msgstr "V našem případě to však dává podmínku:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{PEC}\n"
"& =\n"
"\\alpha(+0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(-0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(-0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(+0.4)\n"
"& = 0.4(\\alpha-\\beta)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{PEC}\n"
"& =\n"
"\\alpha(+0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(-0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(-0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(+0.4)\n"
"& = 0.4(\\alpha-\\beta)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-23
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we use calibration information to relate the observed expectation value to the known ideal one.\n"
msgstr "Nyní použijeme kalibrační informace, abychom propojili pozorovanou očekávanou hodnotu se známou ideální hodnotou.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
